# Brand colors

All visual chrome must use [`lib/core/brand_colors.dart`](lib/core/brand_colors.dart) / `ShadTheme` scheme tokens from the **active** [`BrandPalette`](lib/core/brand_colors.dart) (Settings → Appearance → Color set). No ad-hoc hex for icons, images, borders, shadows, fills, or chart accents.

Default palette **Teal** (others: Ocean, Forest, Slate, Amber). Each palette defines light **and** dark tokens — brightness (ThemeMode) is independent.

| Role | Use |
|------|-----|
| Primary / secondary / border / selection | Active palette via `colorScheme` |
| Gain (numbers up) | `#15803D` / `#4ADE80` — fixed across palettes |
| Loss (numbers down) | `#DC2626` / `#F87171` — fixed across palettes |

## Rules

- Icons / images: `colorScheme.primary` (or secondary well behind them).
- Borders / dividers / inputs: `colorScheme.border` or `input`.
- Shadows: `BrandColors.shadowOf(context)` only (uses active primary).
- Positive/negative **data**: `BrandColors.gainOf` / `lossOf` — never primary for P&L.
- CTAs / focus: primary; soft selected states: secondary.
- Do not hard-code teal hex in new UI — read from theme so palette switching works.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
color: const Color(0xFF16A34A)
boxShadow: [BoxShadow(color: Colors.black26, ...)]

// ✅ GOOD
color: BrandColors.gainOf(context)
boxShadow: [BoxShadow(color: BrandColors.shadowOf(context), ...)]
```
